# rule.forbid.any-price

never declare, store, or pass money as a bare number (dollars or cents), a display string ('$50.37'), or a `{ amount, currency }` bag; never do raw +, -, *, / on money (0.1 + 0.2 = 0.30000000000000004). use the `iso-price` glossary
- store/pass `IsoPriceWords` ('USD 50.37') · structured read `IsoPriceShape` · display-only `IsoPriceHuman` ('$50.37', ui edge)
reach for (price* noun-first): `asIsoPrice(x)` (cast at the boundary, at once) · `priceSum` · `priceSub` · `priceMultiply({ of, by })` · `priceDivide({ of, by })` · `priceAllocate` · `isIsoPrice.equal/.greater/.lesser` (never ===) · `asIsoPriceHuman` for display
allowed: a raw number/string/bag as transient input to asIsoPrice at a boundary
docs: `rhx git.repo.get lines --in ehmpathy/iso-price --paths 'readme.md'` · full rule: rule.require.iso-price
enforcement: money declared as number or display string in a domain object, contract, or stored value = blocker; `{ amount, currency }` bag as the passed shape = blocker; raw arithmetic on money = blocker
